From a21d760dff0e66bd8429bc2eefc1695ac83d5b73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brent Koogler <67485948+jozbee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:11:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Link jaxlib's LAPACK FFI kernels into the CPU PJRT plugin

Vendors jaxlib/cpu/{lapack_kernels,cpu_kernels,ffi_helpers}.* from the
jax-ml/jax repo at the jax-v0.9.0.1 tag (Apache-2.0, same license as
this repo) into a new //jaxlib_cpu_kernels package, trimmed to drop the
sparse/Eigen kernels that aren't needed here. These are the files the
JAX team ships specifically for calling JAX-generated HLO from outside
of JAX/Python: "a C++ user should link against LAPACK directly."

Without this, executables compiled from JAX functions that lower to a
LAPACK-backed custom-call (e.g. jnp.linalg.inv, which needs
lapack_dgetrf_ffi) crash at load/execute time with "No FFI handler
registered for lapack_dgetrf_ffi on a platform Host", since a bare
pjrt_c_api_cpu_plugin.so never registers those handlers the way
jaxlib's Python extension does on import.

Links pjrt_c_api_cpu_plugin.so against the new library plus system
liblapack/libblas.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GTnyeaeFZ8DbU4DgjuVRPi
